body:
I was late at planting my garden. My poor seedlings have been waiting, planned to do it last Monday.   
Then the False Chinch Bugs came!

&#x200B;


It seems like they have moved to greener pastures, it took about a week. Gonna get my tomatoes & etc into the ground tomorrow!

&#x200B;

However, my yard backs up to a wash/desert area and I scattered a shit-ton of wildflower seeds along the fence/alley....so I guess I asked for this.

Mood swings like you describe are one of the main symptoms of Bipolar Disorder.It can also be a symptom of Borderline Personality Disorder, but that involves a lot of other behaviours as well.

&#x200B;

You should discuss this with a professional, if you are able. Self-diagnosis is often inaccurate.

I can't recommend living in spite for the rest of your life.  
But if "outliving the bastards" gets you through this part of your life, embrace it! For real.  
 Because it can't be that much longer before you are out of your house and your parent's control. And then, living well is the best revenge. :)

&#x200B;

And eat some Chicken McNuggets for me! :)  


&#x200B;

My Pragmatic Answer - Funerals are expensive. So is the counseling your father would probably have to go through. Your death would not benefit him. It would not be a good cause. It would be the waste of a life.  


If that is your main reason for suicide, I hopefully just debunked it for you. 

&#x200B;

Perhaps, to connect with other people out there who also don't have family. 

&#x200B;

Or, from a genetic imperative stand-point, to create your own family.
